lthpeak Properties, Inc. is a fully integrated real estate investment trust (REIT) and S&P 500 company. Healthpeak owns, operates, and develops high-quality real estate for healthcare discovery and delivery. Healthpeak Properties, Inc. is based in Denver, Colorado. Healthpeak Properties, Inc. was incorporated in 1985 in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott M. Brinker | President, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 411 people. Revenue per employee of $6.9M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $869K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $35K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Healthpeak Properties, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $14.0B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $357M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 17.55\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 48% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4778151203044392},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DOC Brands Announces Acquisition of MOON Oral Beauty","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/doc-brands-announces-acquisition-of-moon-oral-beauty-302945874.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795108860.0,"origin":"tiingo","senti